---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Show a run's metadata: id, status, timestamps, launcher, and description.

Created, Started and Completed are in the local timezone.

Max Compute Hours and Setup Timeout are the values that the launch requested, when the run has them. One compute hour is one core running for one hour. A run without Max Compute Hours shows Duration instead: the fuzzing time that the launch requested. Elapsed is wall-clock time, which also spans provisioning, setup and teardown. Source is the `antithesis.source` the run was launched from, when the launcher recorded one. Creator is who launched the run: a user, a CI job or an agent. The run also has its user-defined attributes (`attrs.<name>` params at launch) under Attributes, and its repository, branch and commit under Version Control, when the launch recorded them.

An incomplete run also has its failure moment (Failure Hash/VTime), to pass to `runs_logs`, and a failure reason when the run reports one.

Examples:
  runs_show {"run_id": "<run_id>"}

With `json`, the run prints as one JSON object, with its times in RFC 3339 in UTC.
